%3D&orgid=53","verification_status":"verified","career_path_mappings":[{"career_node_id":348,"career_node_slug":"art_social","career_breadcrumb":"Social Sciences & Education","relation":"nearest-parent; plain B.A. has no stated discipline","confidence":"low","mapping_status":"reviewed_with_career_tree_label_issue"}],"mapping_gap":null}],"agent_notes":["The supplied NIRF 2025 College ranking page contains the exact institution name Bhagwan Birsa Munda Government College Pati with city Pati Barwani and state Madhya Pradesh.","The current Madhya Pradesh Higher Education microsite at orgid=53 identifies the Pati campus as Bhagwan Birsa Munda Shaskiya Mahavidyalaya, Pati, District Barwani. The current ePravesh e-Brochure independently identifies the same campus as INS2796, cm_id 677, at First Floor Model School Building, Bokrata Road, Pati, and links back to orgid=53.","The institution microsite's regular-course page lists eight B.A. combinations and its distance-course page lists B.Lib, five M.A. programmes and distance B.A. The regular and distance pages show a 2021 last-update footer; the current ePravesh catalogue confirms a current regular B.A. family with active English Literature, History, Economics, Sociology, Political Science and Hindi Literature branches. Because the institution pages are stale relative to the current admission catalogue and regular PG/diploma sections are empty, the catalogue is marked partial and the record requires manual review.","Duration is null because no official programme page explicitly states duration. Eligibility is included only where the official programme tables state it.","The legacy website link http://www.mphighereducation.nic.in/ins2796 from the District Barwani directory timed out; the current highereducation.mp.gov.in microsite was verified instead.","Normal TLS verification produced the managed proxy's exact self-signed certificate-chain error; --insecure was used only for public GET requests to the expected NIRF, government, Higher Education Department and ePravesh domains.","No third-party aggregator, social profile, Wikipedia page or search snippet was used as verification evidence."]}